+## Routes
+
+Notes on some routes:
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` an ISO instant, `qty` a whole number
+  of dishes). Each dish uses one portion of its recipe; stock is consumed
+  with ref `sale:<ticket>` at `soldAt`. Tickets imported before are skipped.
+  Answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }`: new tickets, and dishes on them
+  (the sum of `qty`). A bad row (`bad_request`) or an item running out
+  (`sale_not_enough_stock`) imports nothing; the message names the row
+  (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers, per item,
+  `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`: theoretical use
+  from sales sold in those days (inclusive, UTC), actual use from every
+  `consume` movement in those days, and `difference` = actual − theoretical.
+  Items with neither are left out.
+
